@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Clustering & Dimensionality Reduction — Selection Map (no labels)
' Synthesis of the unsupervised half: partition the data, or re-coordinate it
' Level:  1

actor "Human expert\nunlabeled data" as H

component "k-means\nhard partition into k groups" as KM <<app>>
component "PCA\nlinear axes of maximum variance" as PCA <<host>>
component "Non-linear embedding\nt-SNE / UMAP" as EMB <<host>>
database  "Downstream use\nfeatures, or a picture" as USE <<db>>

H ARROW_MAIN KM : want group assignments
H ARROW_MAIN PCA : want fewer, uncorrelated features
H ARROW_OPTIONAL EMB : want a 2-D picture\nfor human eyes
KM ARROW_MAIN USE
PCA ARROW_MAIN USE
EMB ARROW_OPTIONAL USE : inspect only — distances\nare not faithful to the input

note bottom of USE
  **Partition vs re-coordinate.** k-means answers
  "which group?"; PCA answers "which directions
  carry the variance?". They compose — PCA first,
  then cluster, is a standard pipeline.
  ----
  **A warning about the pictures.** t-SNE and UMAP
  preserve neighbourhoods, not global distances or
  cluster sizes, so apparent gaps between blobs are
  not evidence. Use them to look, not to conclude.
  ----
  In retrieval systems the same embedding machinery
  becomes an index rather than a plot — see
  ""_spec/study-cases/1-human-expert/rag/vector-dense-rag.puml"".
end note
@enduml
